ould give me more opportunities to create lines. However, sometimes starting with a corner is also good. But since I'm X, and the opponent is O, maybe I should take the center. But wait, the first move is the first turn, so the opponent will be O next. So maybe the best first move is to take the center. Let me check the possible moves. The legal actions are all the cells. So I can choose any. But according to standard strategy, the first move is often the center. So I'll go with (1,1). That's the center. So the action is X(1,1). That should be a good opening move.\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer><|im_end|><|im_start|>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n<|im_end|>"}]
