swer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><X(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by thinking about the best first move in tic-tac-toe. Since the board is empty, I need to choose a position that gives me the best chance to win. The center is usually a good spot because it's part of multiple lines (rows, columns, diagonals). So maybe I should go for the center, which is (1,1). That way, I can potentially create multiple winning opportunities. Alternatively, corners are also good because they are part of two lines each. But the center is more strategic. Let me check the possible moves. The legal actions include X(1,1). So I'll pick that.\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nOkay, let's start by thinking about the best first move in tic-tac-toe. Since the board is empty, I need to choose a position that gives me the best chance to win. The center is usually a good spot because it's part of multiple lines (rows, columns, diagonals). So maybe I should go for the center, which is (1,