k.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><O(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nCHOSEN ACTION:\n<X(2,2)>\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n__X\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,1)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The game is in Turn 2, which is my turn. The current board state is:\n\n___\n___\n__X\n\nSo the third cell of the third row (position 2,2) is X. The legal actions for me are placing an O in any of the remaining cells except (2,2) since it's already taken. My goal is to block the opponent's potential wins and create my own opportunities.\n\nLooking at the board, the X is in the bottom-right corner. The opponent (X) might be trying to form a line. Let me check for possible threats. The X is at (2,2). If they continue to place in (2,1) or (1,2), they could complete a diagonal or a row. But since it's my turn, I need to block any immediate threats.\n\nBut wait, the opponent just placed at (2,2). Let me think about the current state. The board is:\n\nRow 0: all empty\nRow 1: all empty\nRow 2: empty, empty, X\n\nSo the X is in the bottom-right. The possible lines